„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections•…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ;And there was a man of mount Ephraim, whose name was Micah.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙıAnd he said unto his mother, The eleven hundred shekels of silver that were taken from thee, about which thou cursedst, and spakest of also in mine ears, behold, the silver is with me; I took it. And his mother said, Blessed be thou of the LORD, my son.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙüAnd when he had restored the eleven hundred shekels of silver to his mother, his mother said, I had wholly dedicated the silver unto the LORD from my hand for my son, to make a graven image and a molten image: now therefore I will restore it unto thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÔYet he restored the money unto his mother; and his mother took two hundred shekels of silver, and gave them to the founder, who made thereof a graven image and a molten image: and they were in the house of Micah.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€And the man Micah had an house of gods, and made an ephod, and teraphim, and consecrated one of his sons, who became his priest.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbIn those days there was no king in Israel, but every man did that which was right in his own eyes.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsAnd there was a young man out of Beth-lehem-judah of the family of Judah, who was a Levite, and he sojourned there.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§And the man departed out of the city from Beth-lehem-judah to sojourn where he could find a place: and he came to mount Ephraim to the house of Micah, as he journeyed.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“And Micah said unto him, Whence comest thou? And he said unto him, I am a Levite of Beth-lehem-judah, and I go to sojourn where I may find a place.¦layout ªlast_verse	…¤book§chapter«first_verse
